                <pb facs="0199" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/82: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Curtis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-02-15T21:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">February 15,
                                1918, 9 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            February 15, 5.21 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your February 12th, 4 p.m. Minister for Foreign Affairs informs me orally that
                    already Honduranean troops have been withdrawn, as promised, only the usual
                    customs guards remaining. Bonilla says that he is studying all day but will
                    leave earlier than first week in March if possible proceeding via Puerto
                    Cortes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
